{"id":"86a32ef8-b524-4ba7-a575-47a855244a74","workspace_id":"5a4d7682-bc57-4d9d-8696-6144a3546b91","idempotency_key":"r7-cedar-t1-49e1542197474cb083a9b2b823057829","request_hash":"7609a1345fdb304c21263b51a06c35544ded4463f4c529e42cd9552d50377103","status":"FAILED","error_code":"agent_protocol_error","error_message":"Agent tool protocol or evidence report was invalid; execution stopped.","snapshot_revision":4,"snapshot_document_count":4,"conversation_id":"272a699e-fe72-4893-91dd-3c4885071815","conversation_seq":1,"conversation_revision":1,"request":{"mode":"agent","top_k":5,"question":"请比较 Cedar cold-room retrofit 的 Dune 和 Reed。按 controlled trial C-21 的 approved acceptance rule 与 signed measurements，算出两者相对 baseline 的节电百分比，逐项判断 energy reduction 和 maximum interior temperature 是否达标，再给完整的本次试验验收结论并引用依据。","strategy":"bm25","conversation_id":"272a699e-fe72-4893-91dd-3c4885071815","approved_revision":4,"expected_conversation_revision":0},"result":null,"error_result":{"mode":"agent","agent":{"state":"coverage_contract_error","steps":2,"trace":[{"event":"answer_contract","output":{"rule":"no_narrow_ambiguity_rule_matched","scope":"narrow user-message lexical guard; not general referent resolution","choices":[],"version":"evidence-scope-v1","implementation_sha256":"c2d91422685a0d0022ed9099253dcb1449fab091290ad332015945099c5e7bbd","requires_clarification":false,"draft_coverage_verified":false}},{"step":1,"event":"stage_started","phase":"decision","stage_id":"s1","elapsed_ms":15.462,"remaining_ms":74984.538,"parent_stage_id":null},{"step":1,"event":"request_started","phase":"decision","stage_id":"s1","transport":"provider_http","elapsed_ms":15.579,"request_id":"r1","timeout_ms":54984.532,"remaining_ms":74984.421,"request_body_bytes":12059},{"step":1,"event":"request_finished","phase":"decision","usage":{"total_tokens":2245,"prompt_tokens":2189,"completion_tokens":56},"outcome":"returned","stage_id":"s1","transport":"provider_http","elapsed_ms":3243.991,"request_id":"r1","timeout_ms":54984.532,"duration_ms":3228.536,"http_status":200,"usage_known":true,"remaining_ms":71756.009,"response_received":true,"request_body_bytes":12059,"provider_acceptance":"response_received"},{"step":1,"event":"stage_finished","phase":"decision","outcome":"returned","stage_id":"s1","elapsed_ms":3244.163,"duration_ms":3228.708,"remaining_ms":71755.837,"parent_stage_id":null},{"step":1,"event":"model_decision","tools":["search_workspace"],"usage":{"total_tokens":2245,"prompt_tokens":2189,"completion_tokens":56},"clarification_policy":{"rule":"initial_user_scope_clarification_available","scope":"Current user request and completed retrieval only; no semantic ambiguity or evidence sufficiency certification","version":"bounded-evidence-answer-v1","lookup_count":0,"allow_clarification":true,"implementation_sha256":"ab18c50f5619001aad6f9c4c7ec9bc6025e9a92b9ccbc957a55aa556030d4e4f","semantic_ambiguity_verified":false,"evidence_sufficiency_verified":false,"explicit_bounded_answer_request":false}},{"name":"search_workspace","step":1,"event":"stage_started","phase":"tool","stage_id":"s2","elapsed_ms":3244.215,"timeout_ms":71755.68,"remaining_ms":71755.785,"parent_stage_id":null,"request_body_bytes":3395},{"name":"search_workspace","step":1,"event":"tool_started","arguments":{"query":"Cedar cold-room retrofit controlled trial C-21 approved acceptance rule Dune Reed energy reduction maximum interior temperature","top_k":5,"strategy":"bm25"}},{"name":"search_workspace","step":1,"event":"tool","output":{"hits":[{"end":799,"rank":1,"text":"# Cedar cold-room retrofit: approved acceptance rule C-21\nDocument status: approved. Scope: Cedar cold-room retrofit, controlled trial C-21 only.\nAll organizations, equipment, people, dates, and measurements in this document are invented for a synthetic local evaluation. This is not a public source or production record.\nA candidate passes C-21 only if BOTH conditions hold: (1) electrical energy reduction relative to the baseline is at least 12.5 percent; (2) the maximum interior temperature is at most 5.0 degrees Celsius. Use (baseline energy minus candidate energy) divided by baseline energy, times 100. Both inequalities include equality. Do not replace the maximum temperature with the average temperature.\nC-21 establishes trial acceptance only. It does not establish total operating cost","score":10.8686906491,"start":0,"title":"01-approved-acceptance.md","source":"synthetic:cedar/01-approved-acceptance.md","chunk_id":"chunk:fdef1460cd1d9b9eaed6a1de","bm25_score":10.8686906491,"dense_score":null,"document_id":"cedar-1","content_sha256":"a80f0b1e52fabc51e7655955371c4ff1e2b3c6e9e8062dd2b0762d71306fc1dd"},{"end":694,"rank":2,"text":"# Cedar cold-room retrofit: signed C-21 measurements\nDocument status: signed final. Scope: the same 24-hour load profile in controlled trial C-21.\nSynthetic local data; not public-source evidence or production measurements.\nBaseline consumed 240 kWh. Dune consumed 208 kWh; its maximum interior temperature was 5.2 degrees Celsius and its average temperature was 4.1 degrees Celsius. Reed consumed 210 kWh; its maximum interior temperature was 5.0 degrees Celsius and its average temperature was 4.3 degrees Celsius.\nThe trial used the same duration, ambient-temperature profile, and cooling load for all three runs. There were no missing temperature samples. These are the final C-21 readings.","score":6.2753215686,"start":0,"title":"02-signed-trial-readings.md","source":"synthetic:cedar/02-signed-trial-readings.md","chunk_id":"chunk:e47897a4e8901e942eefac05","bm25_score":6.2753215686,"dense_score":null,"document_id":"cedar-2","content_sha256":"bbad144599fee8135abf915db860fad94a845875ef83ea3df8972f4122bf197d"},{"end":563,"rank":3,"text":"# Cedar C-21 operating-cost evidence boundary\nDocument status: final companion note to controlled trial C-21.\nSynthetic local evidence only.\nC-21 measured electricity consumption, not monthly operating cost. Site electricity tariffs, maintenance charges, and equipment lease prices were not collected. No operating-cost comparison between Dune and Reed can be computed from the C-21 package.\nThe signed C-21 measurement sheet and approved C-21 acceptance rule are the sources for trial acceptance. This note supplies no replacement temperature or energy readings.","score":5.4570746441,"start":0,"title":"03-cost-scope-note.md","source":"synthetic:cedar/03-cost-scope-note.md","chunk_id":"chunk:bb83793f0bb82eb2ac1afeae","bm25_score":5.4570746441,"dense_score":null,"document_id":"cedar-3","content_sha256":"59f75a8a9a789dc1ef6bdbd37f6e048fe6d9aa1714e06911b4c56e7c25f3dcfb"},{"end":558,"rank":4,"text":"# Cedar preliminary pilot C-08: superseded readings\nDocument status: superseded preliminary pilot, excluded from C-21 acceptance.\nSynthetic local evidence only.\nIn the earlier C-08 pilot, Dune consumed 200 kWh and its maximum interior temperature was 4.8 degrees Celsius. Reed consumed 220 kWh and its maximum was 5.1 degrees Celsius. The pilot used a different cooling load and duration. Its draft slide called Dune the preferred candidate.\nThese C-08 numbers and that preference do not describe C-21 and must not be substituted for the signed C-21 results.","score":3.55433804,"start":0,"title":"04-superseded-pilot.md","source":"synthetic:cedar/04-superseded-pilot.md","chunk_id":"chunk:9ed8b1d8b88f9ed651fea03d","bm25_score":3.55433804,"dense_score":null,"document_id":"cedar-4","content_sha256":"c7742cd65686fa01ba4621d2956f79db5f85e2a978a781f311ef800552a79fb9"},{"end":843,"rank":5,"text":"rature with the average temperature.\nC-21 establishes trial acceptance only. It does not establish total operating cost or authorize deployment at other locations.","score":2.0978051482,"start":680,"title":"01-approved-acceptance.md","source":"synthetic:cedar/01-approved-acceptance.md","chunk_id":"chunk:da36feaa3d1ecd0df2111cf4","bm25_score":2.0978051482,"dense_score":null,"document_id":"cedar-1","content_sha256":"da4f19c6011acb8b19fcee2c6f00cbdda36f462c462ed5618f59a1c953b5993c"}],"status":"excerpts","passages":{"p0808ce681ca60853":{"quote":"The trial used the same duration, ambient-temperature profile, and cooling load for all three runs. There were no missing temperature samples. These are the final C-21 readings.","chunk_id":"chunk:e47897a4e8901e942eefac05"},"p094e109fe3a2d775":{"quote":"Synthetic local evidence only.","chunk_id":"chunk:bb83793f0bb82eb2ac1afeae"},"p0a0e8c475ad02f5f":{"quote":"In the earlier C-08 pilot, Dune consumed 200 kWh and its maximum interior temperature was 4.8 degrees Celsius. Reed consumed 220 kWh and its maximum was 5.1 degrees Celsius. The pilot used a different cooling load and duration. Its draft slide called Dune the preferred candidate.","chunk_id":"chunk:9ed8b1d8b88f9ed651fea03d"},"p0bc04dbd11f3ceab":{"quote":"All organizations, equipment, people, dates, and measurements in this document are invented for a synthetic local evaluation. This is not a public source or production record.","chunk_id":"chunk:fdef1460cd1d9b9eaed6a1de"},"p0fded7bfff3bf014":{"quote":"Synthetic local data; not public-source evidence or production measurements.","chunk_id":"chunk:e47897a4e8901e942eefac05"},"p246010ce6749e438":{"quote":"C-21 establishes trial acceptance only. It does not establish total operating cost or authorize deployment at other locations.","chunk_id":"chunk:da36feaa3d1ecd0df2111cf4"},"p2ea4779e7ccf26bd":{"quote":"Document status: approved. Scope: Cedar cold-room retrofit, controlled trial C-21 only.","chunk_id":"chunk:fdef1460cd1d9b9eaed6a1de"},"p3383b7fe8d094a7b":{"quote":"A candidate passes C-21 only if BOTH conditions hold: (1) electrical energy reduction relative to the baseline is at least 12.5 percent; (2) the maximum interior temperature is at most 5.0 degrees Celsius. Use (baseline energy minus candidate energy) divided by baseline energy, times 100. Both inequalities include equality. Do not replace the maximum temperature with the average temperature.","chun